WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.137 --> 00:00:01.580
(gentle instrumental music)

00:00:01.580 --> 00:00:03.410
- At this point right now,

00:00:03.410 --> 00:00:05.710
we've just finished the filling process,

00:00:05.710 --> 00:00:08.160
and that drug product is coming over to us

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:11.180
in order to be packed out
into a shipping configuration

00:00:11.180 --> 00:00:13.610
so that we can ship it to
the downstream medical.

00:00:13.610 --> 00:00:15.650
- [Jared] After Merck's
two experimental vaccines

00:00:15.650 --> 00:00:17.800
failed in testing, the drug maker decided

00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:20.010
to play a different role in the pandemic,

00:00:20.010 --> 00:00:22.210
helping rival Johnson and Johnson scale up

00:00:22.210 --> 00:00:24.740
its vaccine manufacturing efforts.

00:00:24.740 --> 00:00:27.800
- That really created a nice
opportunity for us to start

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:29.780
a collaboration with Johnson and Johnson,

00:00:29.780 --> 00:00:32.760
and be able to leverage
their COVID vaccine product

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:34.470
and be able to add capacity

00:00:34.470 --> 00:00:36.810
by leveraging our line in our team.

00:00:36.810 --> 00:00:38.330
- [Jared] Kim Dezura is the plant manager

00:00:38.330 --> 00:00:40.720
at Merck's vaccine manufacturing facility

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:42.500
in West Point, Pennsylvania.

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:44.880
Her plant produces at least 500,000 doses

00:00:44.880 --> 00:00:47.690
of the Johnson and Johnson
COVID vaccine every day.

00:00:47.690 --> 00:00:50.810
And this month J&amp;J released
the first Merck-made shots

00:00:50.810 --> 00:00:53.420
for distribution from
Europe to other countries.

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:56.210
- We're right now on the
manufacturing part of the campus.

00:00:56.210 --> 00:00:58.220
- And it has its own zip code, is that?

00:00:58.220 --> 00:01:00.320
- It does, it does have its own zip code.

00:01:00.320 --> 00:01:02.760
- Public health experts
consider the J&amp;J vaccine

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:06.630
key to protecting underserved
communities around the world.

00:01:06.630 --> 00:01:09.090
The J&amp;J vaccine only requires one dose

00:01:09.090 --> 00:01:10.500
and can be refrigerated,

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:12.350
unlike the Pfizer and Moderna vaccines,

00:01:12.350 --> 00:01:14.890
which need to be stored
at lower temperatures.

00:01:14.890 --> 00:01:16.420
So, how did Merck's West Point plant

00:01:16.420 --> 00:01:18.170
prepare for this immense operation?

00:01:19.030 --> 00:01:21.260
We got an exclusive behind the scenes look

00:01:21.260 --> 00:01:23.783
at what it takes to
manufacture the J&amp;J vaccine.

00:01:24.840 --> 00:01:27.970
So, what's actually
happening here at this plant?

00:01:27.970 --> 00:01:30.210
- The relationship between
Johnson and Johnson

00:01:30.210 --> 00:01:32.760
and Merck have really, two two parts.

00:01:32.760 --> 00:01:35.890
So, we'll be manufacturing,
the drug substance part

00:01:35.890 --> 00:01:38.620
of the vaccine, which is
kind of the active ingredient

00:01:38.620 --> 00:01:39.810
of our vaccine products.

00:01:39.810 --> 00:01:43.270
We'll be doing that in our
Durham, North Carolina facility.

00:01:43.270 --> 00:01:44.860
Here at the West Point site,

00:01:44.860 --> 00:01:47.020
we're responsible for the drug product.

00:01:47.020 --> 00:01:48.730
- [Narrator] Dezura says
that after this facility

00:01:48.730 --> 00:01:51.510
receives the frozen drug substance
from Johnson and Johnson,

00:01:51.510 --> 00:01:55.020
the first step is to store
it here in this freezer room.

00:01:55.020 --> 00:01:56.970
Trevor Brightwell is
the associate director

00:01:56.970 --> 00:02:00.160
of vaccine operations at
the West Point facility.

00:02:00.160 --> 00:02:04.183
- What you see here is
18 minus 70 C freezers.

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:08.180
This is where the drug substance bottles

00:02:08.180 --> 00:02:11.060
will be stored upon receipt to the site.

00:02:11.060 --> 00:02:13.220
- [Jared] Brightwell says
these freezers are all new,

00:02:13.220 --> 00:02:16.030
brought in specifically
to store COVID vaccines

00:02:16.030 --> 00:02:18.660
and each freezer holds 5.5 million doses

00:02:18.660 --> 00:02:19.930
of the drug substance.

00:02:19.930 --> 00:02:21.410
- Your typical freezer in your house

00:02:21.410 --> 00:02:24.420
might be running at minus 10 degrees C.

00:02:24.420 --> 00:02:26.460
These are running at minus 70.

00:02:26.460 --> 00:02:28.540
And so with these types of products,

00:02:28.540 --> 00:02:29.740
the colder that you can keep it,

00:02:29.740 --> 00:02:32.140
it maintains the quality
of the drug substance.

00:02:32.140 --> 00:02:34.210
- [Jared] When the drug
substance is ready to be put

00:02:34.210 --> 00:02:37.450
in the vials, it is moved
to the filling facility.

00:02:37.450 --> 00:02:40.450
Here, the drug is thawed and
then sent to the filling line,

00:02:40.450 --> 00:02:42.630
where exact volumes of
the drug are dispensed

00:02:42.630 --> 00:02:45.410
into glass vials and individually capped

00:02:45.410 --> 00:02:47.660
and once they pass the
automated inspection,

00:02:47.660 --> 00:02:50.460
they're transferred to the pack-out room.

00:02:50.460 --> 00:02:53.070
- So we're in the very
final step of the process,

00:02:53.070 --> 00:02:55.600
right before the product is
about to go out the door.

00:02:55.600 --> 00:02:58.280
- Because vaccines are a
temperature-sensitive product,

00:02:58.280 --> 00:03:01.480
it's important to minimize
their time out of refrigeration.

00:03:01.480 --> 00:03:03.890
So, Merck developed this 3D printed tool

00:03:03.890 --> 00:03:06.050
to help workers pack vials as quickly

00:03:06.050 --> 00:03:08.010
and efficiently as possible.

00:03:08.010 --> 00:03:10.610
This tool grabs 39 vials in one go,

00:03:10.610 --> 00:03:13.850
so workers don't have to
load the vials one at a time.

00:03:13.850 --> 00:03:15.590
After the vials are ready to go,

00:03:15.590 --> 00:03:17.380
they are shipped back
to Johnson and Johnson

00:03:17.380 --> 00:03:19.730
to handle the final
packaging and distribution.

00:03:20.710 --> 00:03:23.390
Preparing for this operation
involved getting new equipment

00:03:23.390 --> 00:03:26.930
and modifying its filling line
to accommodate the J&amp;J vials,

00:03:26.930 --> 00:03:29.950
all of which Merck says it
accomplished in less than a year.

00:03:29.950 --> 00:03:33.390
How long does it normally get
ready to manufacture vaccines

00:03:33.390 --> 00:03:34.540
and do this process?

00:03:34.540 --> 00:03:36.710
- Typically, if we're
bringing in a new product

00:03:36.710 --> 00:03:39.330
to a filling line, it
might take, you know,

00:03:39.330 --> 00:03:41.700
a year or two to be able
to really go through

00:03:41.700 --> 00:03:45.660
all the qualifications
and the transfer details.

00:03:45.660 --> 00:03:47.190
- [Jared] Part of the reason
Merck says it was able

00:03:47.190 --> 00:03:50.210
to adapt in just a few months,
was it's almost 60 years

00:03:50.210 --> 00:03:52.900
of vaccine manufacturing experience.

00:03:52.900 --> 00:03:54.010
- We have a long history

00:03:54.010 --> 00:03:56.020
and a lot of different
types of vaccine products,

00:03:56.020 --> 00:03:58.180
including you know, products
that are pretty similar

00:03:58.180 --> 00:04:00.510
to the Johnson and Johnson products.

00:04:00.510 --> 00:04:02.740
So, it really helped
us to be able to adapt

00:04:02.740 --> 00:04:05.190
our current procedures quickly.

00:04:05.190 --> 00:04:06.990
- [Jared] Another reason
is that Merck received help

00:04:06.990 --> 00:04:08.460
from the U.S. government.

00:04:08.460 --> 00:04:11.120
In March, the Department of
Health and Human Services

00:04:11.120 --> 00:04:13.300
said it would spend $105 million

00:04:13.300 --> 00:04:15.810
to help Merck upgrade its facilities.

00:04:15.810 --> 00:04:19.510
- A typical part for a
filling line may take months

00:04:19.510 --> 00:04:21.350
to receive and we were
able to turn that around

00:04:21.350 --> 00:04:23.780
in sometimes days and weeks.

00:04:23.780 --> 00:04:25.710
- [Jared] Dezura says Merck
plans to continue partnering

00:04:25.710 --> 00:04:27.870
with J&amp;J until the pandemic ends

00:04:27.870 --> 00:04:30.850
or its manufacturing capabilities
are no longer needed.

00:04:30.850 --> 00:04:33.660
- I think all of us have
been touched by the pandemic

00:04:33.660 --> 00:04:36.680
and so the ability to really contribute

00:04:36.680 --> 00:04:40.221
a potential solution for that
is, is just really remarkable.

00:04:40.221 --> 00:04:43.888
(gentle instrumental music)

